# StrikeNova frontend — environment configuration
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL — the backend API origin, inlined into the client
# bundle at BUILD TIME. It is the single source of truth for REST (axios
# baseURL), WebSocket (chainWsUrl derives ws/wss from it), and the OAuth
# callback/origin derivations in the settings page.
#
# PRODUCTION BUILDS REQUIRE IT — fail closed (ADR-015):
#   a production build (NODE_ENV=production) with a missing, blank,
#   whitespace-only, non-URL, plain-http, localhost/loopback, or historical-
#   Railway value FAILS with a clear configuration error. No fallback
#   backend URL is provided.
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.example.com
#
# Local development / tests (optional): leave unset for relative-URL mode,
# or point at a local backend (http/localhost allowed outside production):
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000
